wh40k-footfall-faction-kasballica = Kasballica Mission
wh40k-footfall-kasballica-marker-desc = Persistent Kasballica NPC source. Rotate the arrow to the desired facing before map initialization.
wh40k-footfall-npc-kasballicaofficer-name = Oliva Krakovskaya
wh40k-footfall-npc-kasballicaofficer-desc = A Kasballica Mission representative. Welcoming in conversation, she remembers both your words and the pauses between them.
wh40k-footfall-npc-kasballicamerchant-name = Leman Londoron
wh40k-footfall-npc-kasballicamerchant-desc = A Kasballica Mission dealer in a black cap. Happy to discuss an item's condition; less forthcoming about its previous owner.
wh40k-footfall-ambient-kasballicaammunitionworker-name = Kasballica ammunition worker
wh40k-footfall-ambient-kasballicaammunitionworker-desc = A Kasballica associate inspects an ammunition batch at the workbench. Conversation never makes them lose count.
wh40k-footfall-ambient-kasballicaguard-name = Kasballica guard
wh40k-footfall-ambient-kasballicaguard-desc = A Kasballica guard in a Moebian-6 helmet and bulletproof vest. Holds a stub pistol and watches the corridor closely.
wh40k-footfall-marker-kasballicaofficer-name = Marker: Oliva Krakovskaya, Kasballica officer
wh40k-footfall-marker-kasballicamerchant-name = Marker: Leman Londoron, Kasballica merchant
wh40k-footfall-marker-kasballicaammunitionworker-name = Kasballica ammunition worker marker
wh40k-footfall-marker-kasballicaguard-name = Kasballica guard marker
wh40k-footfall-merchant-kasballica-title = Leman Londoron — Mission stock
wh40k-footfall-merchant-kasballica-intro = Weapons, ammunition, equipment, and occasionally something from farther afield. Check the current batch: rumours take up no shelf space.
wh40k-footfall-dialogue-kasballicaofficer-intro = Oliva Krakovskaya. I represent the Kasballica Mission's interests on Footfall. If you have a proposal, take a seat. If you have a rumour, take one anyway; sometimes they amount to the same thing.
wh40k-footfall-dialogue-kasballicaofficer-menu = What would you like to know? We'll leave our clients' names out of this conversation. They pay for that.
wh40k-footfall-dialogue-kasballicaofficer-mission-choice = What does the Mission do?
wh40k-footfall-dialogue-kasballicaofficer-mission-reply = The Kasballica brings together criminal interests from Calixis. Its Mission here connects suppliers, carriers, and buyers. One needs a reliable route; another needs a buyer who asks fewer questions. We find both and take our share. Chance acquaintances are cheaper only until the first ship disappears.
wh40k-footfall-dialogue-kasballicaofficer-coldtrade-choice = What is the Cold Trade?
wh40k-footfall-dialogue-kasballicaofficer-coldtrade-reply = It means dealing in forbidden xenos artefacts and technology. A convenient name: cold sounds calmer than heretical. For us it involves buyers, transport, and risk; an Imperial investigator would describe it differently. Have an alien object assessed before buying it, rather than after it starts answering your thoughts.
wh40k-footfall-dialogue-kasballicaofficer-footfall-choice = Why Footfall?
wh40k-footfall-dialogue-kasballicaofficer-footfall-reply = Expeditions, Rogue Traders, hired captains, and people with very flexible manifests meet here. A useful place for a broker. Footfall tolerates a great deal until someone else's profits or the local order suffer. Don't mistake that for safety: every quiet corridor has someone paying to keep it quiet.
wh40k-footfall-dialogue-kasballicaofficer-trust-choice = How are deals made here?
wh40k-footfall-dialogue-kasballicaofficer-trust-reply = State the goods, the route, and the terms. Promise what you can deliver. Leave other people's cargo out of canteen conversation. A reputation grows slowly and can vanish in one boastful speech. Leman handles the counter; I discuss the Mission's contacts and interests. I prefer agreements to threats: at least you can reread them.
wh40k-footfall-dialogue-kasballicaofficer-charters-choice = Are you part of the Chartist Fleet?
wh40k-footfall-dialogue-kasballicaofficer-charters-reply = No. Chartist captains carry cargo along their permitted routes; we arrange deals where a charter alone is insufficient. We might hire a carrier or negotiate with a Rogue Trader. Working alongside someone does not make us the same organisation. On Footfall, remember that especially when signing papers.
wh40k-footfall-dialogue-kasballicaofficer-farewell = Come back with a clear proposal. Leave the fog to the navigators; they charge separately for it.
wh40k-footfall-dialogue-kasballicamerchant-intro = Leman Londoron. I check condition and calibre; I don't investigate the ancestry of every cartridge case. What are you looking for?
wh40k-footfall-dialogue-kasballicamerchant-menu = You can inspect the batch, or first ask what fits what. The second option is usually cheaper.
wh40k-footfall-dialogue-kasballicamerchant-stock-choice = What do you sell?
wh40k-footfall-dialogue-kasballicamerchant-stock-reply = Stub pistols, magazines, ammunition boxes, work clothes, and vests. Sometimes alien equipment turns up, such as a Tau pulse pistol. It's priced apart from ordinary hardware and isn't in every batch. The counter tells you availability and price, rather than my assistant's promises.
wh40k-footfall-dialogue-kasballicamerchant-ammunition-choice = Which ammunition do I need?
wh40k-footfall-dialogue-kasballicamerchant-ammunition-reply = The ordinary stub pistol uses its own magazine and 10 mm cartridges. The heavy model has a different magazine and its own ammunition: sharing the word stub guarantees nothing. The Tau pistol uses its internal charge, not our cartridge boxes. Check the labels. Our worker at the bench notices an extra case faster than I notice an extra zero on an invoice.
wh40k-footfall-dialogue-kasballicamerchant-discretion-choice = What about the goods' provenance?
wh40k-footfall-dialogue-kasballicamerchant-discretion-reply = Ask all you like about technical condition. Yesterday's cargo route is a question for Oliva, preferably away from the corridor. The Mission connects sellers with buyers; that doesn't make alien goods permissible. Your money buys the item, not indulgence from Imperial authorities.
wh40k-footfall-dialogue-kasballicamerchant-farewell = Check your purchases before departure. An empty magazine makes a poor debating partner far from Footfall.
wh40k-footfall-ambient-kasballicaammunitionworker-line-1 = Forty rounds per box. Count thirty-nine and the customer notices. Count forty-one and Leman notices.
wh40k-footfall-ambient-kasballicaguard-line-1 = The corridor is open. Someone else's storeroom isn't. Somehow, that distinction needs explaining every day.
wh40k-footfall-ambient-kasballicaammunitionworker-line-2 = The Chartists have papers for every box. We have boxes for every paper. Keeps the desk level.
wh40k-footfall-ambient-kasballicaguard-line-2 = I guard the door, not the mysteries of existence. Ask Oliva about those. Knock first.
wh40k-footfall-ambient-kasballicaammunitionworker-line-3 = Case, primer, inspection. The difficult part is explaining why coffee isn't an ammunition ingredient.
wh40k-footfall-ambient-kasballicaguard-line-3 = If you're here for Leman, say you're shopping. Someone came looking for truth yesterday. Stayed all evening without buying a thing.
wh40k-footfall-ambient-kasballicaammunitionworker-line-4 = Leman wants the batch finished faster. I offered to count faster. Fortunately, the cartridges took no offence.
wh40k-footfall-ambient-kasballicaguard-line-4 = The quietest shift is when everyone remembers whose crates they're carrying. Especially first-time carriers.
wh40k-footfall-ambient-kasballicaammunitionworker-line-5 = I checked that batch already. Now I'm checking whether someone carried it off while I inspected the next one.
wh40k-footfall-ambient-kasballicaguard-line-5 = Good helmet. Stops a blow. Hasn't stopped a conversation about discounts yet.
wh40k-footfall-ambient-kasballicaammunitionworker-line-6 = Keep alien things off my bench. One was glowing without power yesterday. We have enough overtime of our own.
wh40k-footfall-ambient-kasballicaguard-line-6 = Our cargo moves quietly. That's no invitation to sneak; ordinary footsteps give me less work.

